00:19:34.900 --> 00:19:36.020
What did you two fight about?

00:19:36.590 --> 00:19:37.890
Oh, that it was nothing.

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:40.540
I'd been going out without the linden for a long time,

00:19:40.560 --> 00:19:42.240
and she had ideas she could cut me out.

00:19:42.340 --> 00:19:43.360
You know how girls are.

00:19:43.920 --> 00:19:48.720
Oh, I must get some thread for this hem.

00:20:18.490 --> 00:20:20.090
We've worked long enough tonight.

00:20:20.930 --> 00:20:22.410
I'm getting sleepy anyhow, aren't you?

00:20:23.260 --> 00:20:25.120
Yes, it's been quite a day.

00:20:26.820 --> 00:20:28.140
Will Mr. North be out late?

00:20:29.510 --> 00:20:29.970
Yes, he's out.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:32.120
a publisher's dinner. I never know what time

00:20:32.120 --> 00:20:33.520
he'll come in when he's out with the boys.

00:20:34.400 --> 00:20:36.580
Well, good night. You know where your room is.

00:20:36.620 --> 00:20:38.600
Sleep tight. You too, Mrs. North.

00:20:38.900 --> 00:20:41.060
Well, call me Pam. Thank you, Pam.

00:20:41.440 --> 00:20:41.780
Good night.

00:22:01.720 --> 00:22:03.220
Open this door.

00:22:04.790 --> 00:22:07.250
Ronnie, you were the one in the fashion racket, not Cynthia.

00:22:07.660 --> 00:22:08.740
And you killed her.

00:22:09.740 --> 00:22:12.380
I said open that door, Mrs. North.

00:22:13.840 --> 00:22:15.440
Found the camera in your hatbox.

00:22:15.600 --> 00:22:16.560
You know that now, don't you?

00:22:16.600 --> 00:22:17.940
And that's why you're trying to get out of here.

00:22:20.330 --> 00:22:21.730
You're a very good actress, Ronnie.

00:22:22.600 --> 00:22:26.140
Your stereo over Cynthia and your fear of the apartment were very convincing.

00:22:26.860 --> 00:22:28.940
You don't open that door.

00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:29.960
There's only one.

00:22:31.080 --> 00:22:32.900
Ronnie, put those digits down!

00:23:02.970 --> 00:23:04.150
All right, I'm through.

00:23:07.740 --> 00:23:11.320
I'm glad, honey.

00:23:13.410 --> 00:23:13.670
It's not.

00:23:15.500 --> 00:23:18.660
It's like standing under a shower after a hot, dirty day.

00:23:21.040 --> 00:23:25.440
I got tangled into the racket of photographing Madam Susie's originals.

00:23:26.490 --> 00:23:29.960
I liked originals, too, in Dollar...

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:38.080
bills i only used cynthia to deliver the film to the buyer but then i thought she started to get wise

00:23:38.080 --> 00:23:46.280
and i was afraid of her taking the deal away from you know the rest

00:24:11.480 --> 00:24:13.060
Yes, sir.

00:24:15.320 --> 00:24:15.480
Me.

00:24:16.740 --> 00:24:17.180
Yes, sir.

00:24:18.810 --> 00:24:19.450
Would you like it?

00:24:20.920 --> 00:24:22.120
The first day I saw you.

00:24:23.660 --> 00:24:24.500
There's something different.

00:24:25.850 --> 00:24:26.610
But the hair.

00:24:27.430 --> 00:24:27.730
No.

00:24:30.800 --> 00:24:31.340
New shoes.

00:24:32.180 --> 00:24:32.520
No.

00:24:34.160 --> 00:24:34.940
The dress.

00:24:35.280 --> 00:24:35.520
Yeah.

00:24:38.440 --> 00:24:39.240
Paid for them.

00:24:41.280 --> 00:24:41.900
How much was it?

00:24:44.870 --> 00:24:45.710
$29.95.

00:24:47.460 --> 00:24:47.840
Sold.

